before:
Create Cargo.toml containing [package], name = "study-lib", version = "0.1.0", edition = "2024" on separate lines. In tests/public.rs put the following external-crate test, then run cargo test --offline. The package hyphen becomes an underscore in the Rust crate path. Unit tests can reach private implementation details; integration tests consume exported items.
```rust
#[test]
fn upper_boundary() {
    assert_eq!(study_lib::clamp(11), 10);
}
```

Complete local Rust example; the app itself does not execute it:
```rust
pub fn clamp(n: i32) -> i32 { n.clamp(0, 10) }

#[cfg(test)]
mod tests {
    use super::clamp;
    #[test]
    fn lower_boundary() { assert_eq!(clamp(-1), 0); }
}

```

after:
Follow the labeled parts of this example.
```rust
// File: Cargo.toml
[package]
name = "study-lib"
version = "0.1.0"
edition = "2024"

// File: tests/public.rs
#[test]
fn upper_boundary() { assert_eq!(study_lib::clamp(11), 10); }

// File: src/lib.rs
pub fn clamp(n: i32) -> i32 { n.clamp(0, 10) }

#[cfg(test)]
mod tests {
    use super::clamp;
    #[test]
    fn lower_boundary() { assert_eq!(clamp(-1), 0); }
}
```
